# UI

## Menus inside dialogs

A `.modal` scrolls its own content (`overflow: auto`), so anything that sticks out of it is clipped. A `details[data-menu]` opened inside a dialog (USE PROMPT in the Fix dialog) would hide under the dialog's edge.

- `public/app.js` pins those menus to the viewport on `toggle`: `position: fixed`, lined up with the summary's right edge. `.up` menus open upward unless there's no room above.
- Don't fix clipping with `overflow: visible` on `.modal`. Tall dialogs on phones need to scroll.
- Don't add `transform` to `.modal` or its parents. A transform makes `position: fixed` relative to the dialog again, and the menu gets clipped.

## Other gotchas

- Dialogs open non-modal on localhost (`openDialog` in app.js), so element pickers can reach them. Check both: `.modal[open]:not(:modal)` styles the local case.
- The CSP is `script-src 'self'`: no inline `onclick` or `<script>`. Add behaviour to `app.js` with a `data-*` hook (for example `data-confirm` on a form).
- `app.js` wires tooltips and area focus to the first `[data-grid]` on the page. The small readout grid (`.grid.mini`) must not carry `data-grid`.
- `details[data-menu]` gets closing on outside click and Escape for free. Reuse it for popovers (`.note`) instead of new JS.
